    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d361">

                <pb facs="0939" n="905" sameAs="frus:frus1947v02/pg905"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Germany)/12–2447:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Political Adviser for Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Murphy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-12-24T16:00:00+01:00">December 24,
                            1947—4 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3786. Personal for Gallman. There seems to
                    be surprising discrepancy between the viewpoint attributed to Kirkpatrick<anchor n="3" xml:id="d361-f1"/>
                    and our understanding of Mr. Bevin’s
                    views, particularly Kirkpatrick’s
                    opinion that central government should be established promptly, presumably at
                    Frankfurt.</p>
                <p>On subject of payment of reparations to the Soviet Union, we, of course, do not
                    agree with Kirkpatrick’s view that the
                    Russians should be appeased in order to obtain respect for the Four-Power
                    agreement which authorizes the powers to occupy sectors in the greater Berlin
                    area.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 3786, to Moscow as 598, for London as 464.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Murphy</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d361-f1" n="3" xml:id="d361-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram 6607, December 23, from London, <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
